{"resourceIdentifier":"4620","resourceName":"14 MW Waste-to-Energy Project by Antony Lara Renewable Energy Pvt. Ltd","description":"The project activity is 14MW Waste to Energy Power Plant located at Moshi Kachara Depot, Pimpri, Pune, India. The plant utilizes Refuse-Derived Fuel (“RDF”) as feedstock derived from the separation and sorting of Municipal Solid Waste (“MSW”) excluding the recyclable or potentially hazardous materials from the waste stream. The MSW will be sourced from the Pimpri Chinchwad Municipality area as per the concession agreement with Pimpri Chinchwad Municipal Corporation.\r\nThe main purpose of this project activity is to generate clean form of electricity through waste to energy-based power generation. The project will treat about 700 ton of RDF per day and generate electricity with the installed capacity of 14 MW. The project activity helps to avoid methane emissions from open dump site iand generate renewable electricity, which displaced part of the electricity otherwise supplied by grid connected power plants. The expected average emission reduction from the project is 65,318 tCO2e annually.","location":{"latitude":18.658196,"longitude":73.857354},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":{"startInclusive":"2023-11-21","endExclusive":"2023-12-22","endInclusive":"2023-12-21"},"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"4620"}]},{"code":"STATE_PROVINCE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Maharashtra"}]}],"participationSummaries":[{"programCode":"VCS","attributes":[{"code":"PROPONENT_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Antony Lara Renewable Energy Pvt. Ltd"},{"type":"string","value":"India"},{"type":"string","value":"02242130300"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_STATUS","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Registered"}]},{"code":"EST_ANNUAL_EMISSION_REDCT","values":[{"type":"string","value":"61304"}]},{"code":"PRIMARY_PROJECT_CATEGORY_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Waste handling and disposal"}]},